From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 1270 redfin: /dev/vmmu, page tables for the Venus SMMU bank
 (zero-copy video buffers), kern.sweet_vmmu (default 0 = off)

venus-iommu. Venus only sees the fixed 1057 window (IOVA = PA, 2 MB blocks) of the
bank venusctl/venusd set up in userland; every frame is copied through /dev/pmem.
/dev/vmmu (clone node, one minor per open) adds 4 KB page mappings of any memory
to that bank: L1 slots 0-1 (IOVA 0-2 GB) point at kernel-owned L2/L3 tables
(cached kernel pages, cleaned to PoC), the window (slot 2) stays userland's.
VMMU_MAP pins a user range (IOMemoryDescriptor prepare, as BoImport) or retains
an IOSurface by id (SweetSurface memory), maps it at a free IOVA in
0x40000000-0x80000000 (or a fixed one from 0x01000000), TLBIASID + TLBSYNC.
VMMU_UNMAP / client close: PTEs cleared, TLB flushed, then pages released.
VMMU_SYNC: clean / clean+invalidate by physical page (Venus is not IO-coherent).
VMMU_STATUS: maps, bytes, FSR/FAR/FSYNR0 + faulting SID (also logged once per
new fault at every call). RW sysctl kern.sweet_vmmu: 0 (default) refuses ATTACH
and MAP = today's behaviour; 1 on.

Klog: "SWEET VMMU: /dev/vmmu ready", "attached to CBn ...", "client n closed:
N mappings unmapped", "CBn fault FSR ... SID ...".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC4L8fevHSDuAPRVwdU
---
